messages:
Nia: quick proposal: split the big structured-output doc into two smaller PRs to make reviews faster. PR A = JSON Schemas + compact examples. PR B = runtime parsing patterns, SDK snippets, and fallback heuristics. i'll open both and assign owners.

Diego: i'll take PR A (schemas + examples). plan: move examples into docs/schemas/, add nullable-array and union-array compact examples, and include a tiny JSON Schema validation snippet.

Priya: i'll own PR B (parsing + SDK). going to add: tryParse envelope snippet for SDK 4.x, a minimal regex fallback for badly-formed outputs, and short notes on when to use function calling vs structured output.

Owen: suggestion: keep reusable SDK snippets under docs/parsers/snippets so other pages can import them. also include a one-line migration comparison for SDK 3.x -> 4.x call payloads.

Tess: i'll run a link audit and prepare redirects for moved paths. if PR A lands first, i'd like to land redirects immediately after so no broken links on main.

LintBot: Found issues: some fenced code blocks missing language tag; one JSON example has trailing comma. These will fail CI until fixed.

Nia: timeline: drafts tomorrow, aim to merge both by Friday. ping if blocked.

Diego: PR A opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/912. moved examples and added frontmatter. left TODO for the validation snippet.

Priya: PR B draft: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/913. includes SDK 4.x envelope fallback and a short regex fallback. flagged wording around PII safety for review.

Owen: reviewing PR 912 now. small editorial nits, but structure looks good.

Diego: fixed lint nit and added JSON Schema validation sample using ajv in the examples folder. repushed.

Tess: opened redirects PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/914. includes sidebar updates and a tiny redirect map.

Priya: updated PR 913 to follow the snippet location Owen suggested and shortened the fallback example. code sample:```js
// SDK 4.x minimal parse fallback
try {
  const out = JSON.parse(text);
  return out;
} catch (e) {
  const m = /"result"\s*:\s*"([^\"]+)"/.exec(text);
  return m ? {result: m[1]} : {raw: text, parseError: true};
}
```

LintBot: CI passed for PR 912 after lint fixes. PR 913 has one doc-style nit.

Diego: merged PR 912 (schemas + examples).

Priya: merged PR 913 after addressing the doc nit and adding the SDK migration blurb.

Tess: merged redirects PR 914 and updated changelog.

ReleaseNotesBot: Added release note: "Docs: split structured-output guidance into schema and parsing sections; added SDK 4.x parsing fallback examples and redirects."

Nia: awesome, thanks everyone. closing this split-and-move thread. :tada:
